00:42:16.080 --> 00:42:17.640
but I think empirically there's a lot

00:42:17.640 --> 00:42:20.390
of evidence that there's huge temptations

00:42:20.390 --> 00:42:23.310
from the national security
establishment in Europe

00:42:23.310 --> 00:42:25.280
and in the United States
I think increasingly

00:42:25.280 --> 00:42:27.870
framing level international
policy of the next 20 years.

00:42:27.870 --> 00:42:29.770
- There's no doubt about that.

00:42:29.770 --> 00:42:31.461
I mean, I can see that entirely,

00:42:31.461 --> 00:42:35.299
but that they're not actually
the political leadership,

00:42:35.299 --> 00:42:37.891
they're supposed to be subordinate to it.

00:42:37.891 --> 00:42:40.130
But no you're of course you're right

00:42:40.130 --> 00:42:43.221
that these forces are active and you know,

00:42:43.221 --> 00:42:47.710
the national security
expertise being quite far

00:42:47.710 --> 00:42:50.190
beyond militaries is
always seeking enemies.

00:42:50.190 --> 00:42:53.540
As you say, I think
the real dilemma is how

00:42:53.540 --> 00:42:56.850
to free development assistance

00:42:56.850 --> 00:43:01.540
